{"schema_version": 4, "name": "mosaic_amine_crossfeeding", "created": "2026-11-21", "status": "planned", "execution_status": "planned", "phase": "Design", "runtime": {"default_emitter": "xarray"}, "executive": {"question": "Can biogenic-amine cross-feeding between Gardnerella and Lactobacillus, coupled to vaginal pH, produce the bistable healthy/BV community states that the amine data (Borgogna 2021, Puebla-Barragan 2021) imply?", "verdict": "Yes \u2014 the mechanistic ODE is bistable: a protective acidic Lactobacillus state (amines cleared, pH < 4.5) and a BV state (Gardnerella-dominant, ~mM amine pool, pH > 5.5), separated by the amine-inhibition / amine-degradation feedback."}, "scientific_argument": "Two BV papers quantify opposite arms of a biogenic-amine loop. Borgogna et al. 2021 (doi:10.1128/aem.03068-20) show Gardnerella-associated amines inhibit Lactobacillus growth (putrescine 3,179 \u00b5M \u2192 +22-33% doubling time) and suppress lactic-acid production; Puebla-Barragan et al. 2021 (doi:10.3390/ijms222212279) show Lactobacillus degrades those amines and grows faster at low pH. Closing the loop \u2014 amines \u22a3 Lactobacillus growth & lactate \u2192 pH rises \u2192 favours Gardnerella, vs Lactobacillus \u2192 lactate \u2192 low pH & faster amine degradation \u2192 clears amines \u2014 predicts bistability, which this ODE reproduces.", "readouts": [{"name": "lactobacillus", "store_path": "stores.species.Lactobacillus", "description": "Lactobacillus relative abundance (protective / lactic-acid state)", "units": "relative abundance", "status": "available"}, {"name": "gardnerella", "store_path": "stores.species.Gardnerella", "description": "Gardnerella relative abundance (BV-associated, amine producer)", "units": "relative abundance", "status": "available"}, {"name": "amines", "store_path": "stores.species.Amines", "description": "Biogenic-amine pool (putrescine-equivalent)", "units": "\u00b5M", "status": "available"}, {"name": "lactate", "store_path": "s